    "wl_image_text_cta_za6tW4": {
      "type": "wl-image-text-cta",
      "blocks": {
        "image_ipYjV6": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/mct-oil-cbd.png",
            "bkg_color": "#595378",
            "font_color": "#ffffff",
            "tagline": "",
            "title": "What Is MCT Oil?",
            "content": "<p>MCT oil (medium-chain triglyceride oil) is a highly digestible oil typically derived from coconuts that is commonly used as a carrier oil in CBD tinctures. Because CBD is fat-soluble, it binds naturally with MCT oil, helping improve absorption and delivery within the body. MCT oil is flavor-neutral, shelf-stable, and easily metabolized, making it an ideal base for CBD products. Together, CBD and MCT oil create a convenient, effective tincture that supports consistent dosing and optimal cannabinoid absorption.</p>",
            "cta_text": "",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        },
        "image_Cam9hg": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/sublingual-cbd.png",
            "bkg_color": "#ffd700",
            "font_color": "#010101",
            "tagline": "",
            "title": "Sublingual vs. Other Delivery Methods",
            "content": "<p>Sublingual CBD tinctures are one of the most effective ways to take CBD, delivering hemp-derived cannabinoids directly through the tissues under the tongue for fast absorption. By holding CBD oil under your tongue for 30–60 seconds before swallowing, you may experience a quicker onset and higher bioavailability compared to CBD gummies, edibles, or CBD-infused beverages. Because sublingual CBD bypasses much of the digestive process, more of the CBD may be available for your body to use. This makes CBD tinctures a popular choice for those seeking fast-acting, reliable support for relaxation, stress management, sleep, and overall wellness.</p>",
            "cta_text": "",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        },
        "image_GP3xtF": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/broad-spectrum-cbd.png",
            "bkg_color": "#bcd868",
            "font_color": "#010101",
            "tagline": "",
            "title": "Full-Spectrum CBD VS ^THC-Free Broad-Spectrum",
            "content": "<p><strong>Full-spectrum CBD</strong> contains CBD along with other naturally occurring hemp compounds, including cannabinoids, terpenes, flavonoids, and trace amounts of THC (less than 0.3%). These compounds work together in what is often called the \"entourage effect,\" which may enhance the overall benefits of the hemp extract.</p><p><strong>THC-free broad-spectrum CBD</strong> also contains multiple cannabinoids and beneficial hemp compounds but has undergone additional processing to remove all detectable THC. This makes broad-spectrum CBD a popular option for those who want the benefits of a multi-cannabinoid hemp extract without consuming THC. Whether you choose full-spectrum or THC-free broad-spectrum CBD, both offer a convenient way to support relaxation, recovery, sleep, and overall wellness with hemp-derived cannabinoids.</p><p>For more a detailed rundown of the differences between full-spectrum and broad-spectrum check out <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/comparing-cbd-isolate-full-spectrum-and-broad-spectrum-cbd-which-is-right-for-you?_pos=1&_psq=broad-spectrum&_ss=e&_v=1.0\" title=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/comparing-cbd-isolate-full-spectrum-and-broad-spectrum-cbd-which-is-right-for-you?_pos=1&_psq=broad-spectrum&_ss=e&_v=1.0\">this article.</a></p>",
            "cta_text": "",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        }
      },
